  "summary": "Highlights\n\n2011 – Present\nDatabase Developer assigned to develop  a relational Database Schema for the Health Care Record management. Wrote an ETL to transfer live data from an object oriented database to a  relational  reporting database in real time mode.\n\n2010 – 2011\nSoftware Developer assigned to the HDM Cerepont team.   This team is charged with the task of bringing together two platforms HDM and Clintrac into one. I am currently working on a Web solution using XBAP, Silverlight, Javascript, connecting through an IIS server. The database is MS 2005/2008. Also responsible for final line of support for our HDM software product line.\n\n\n2007-2009\nDatabase developer for the Bench Marking reporting product.  The database supports  ICD9 and ICD10 codes and many inpatient groupers. \nMajor responsibilities included gathering specifications for GPS and Codefinder groupers. Assisted in building the MSSQL database schema and populating it with the supporting data. Modularized to support specific countries. Additional US add-ons such as  Responsible for writing a detailed maintenance plan and assisting others writing SQL queries for reports. I was responsible for final line of support for HDM.\n\n2006-2007\nModified the Performance Analytical Reporting Software (PARM) to handle the processing and  reporting of multiple groupers. I was responsible for final line of support for HDM.\n\n\n2000 – 2005 \nTechnical lead for 8 to 11 software engineers over seeing all development efforts. Major responsibilities included implementing a new database platform, Microsoft SQL Server 2000/2005, increasing our record size to eliminate the 32k restriction and implementing the HIPAA requirements into the software. I used techniques as ADO record binding, prepared statements and stored procedures to increase performance. I also, assisted other engineers in completing their assignment. Responsible for final line of support for HDM.\n\nSpecialties: TECHNICAL SKILLS \nProgramming: C, C++, C# & Others\nDatabase: Pervasive, SQL Server 2000/2005/2008, ADO, ADO.NET,  Stored Procedures \nDevelopment Platforms: Borland, Visual Studio \nPlatforms: Windows, Windows Servers",
